/-- Concavity and nonnegativity force the chord joining `(0,1)` to the
limiting endpoint `(M,0)` to lie below the graph. No endpoint continuity
at `M` is required. -/
theorem concave_reference_lower_bound {M : ℝ} (hM : 0 < M) {u : ℝ → ℝ}
